#, no-wrap
msgid "Leverage trim SQD for improved configuration selection for the latest version of Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"
msgstr "Manfaatkan trim SQD untuk pemilihan konfigurasi yang lebih baik bagi versi terkini Pepenyahpepenjuruan kuantum berasaskan sampel (SQD)"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Leverage trim SQD for improved configuration selection"
msgstr "Manfaatkan trim SQD untuk pemilihan konfigurasi yang lebih baik"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/trim-sqd.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The default behavior of [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion) is to diagonalize each subsampled batch and keep the best result. **Trim SQD** instead treats the batches as candidates to be screened: each is diagonalized, *trimmed* down to the configurations carrying the largest weight, and the survivors of all the batches are merged and diagonalized together. That merged diagonalization is the one whose energy the iteration reports, and its own trimmed output seeds the next iteration.\n"
msgstr "Tingkah laku lalai [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion) ialah menyahpepenjuruankan setiap kelompok subsampel dan menyimpan hasil terbaik. **Trim SQD** sebaliknya menganggap kelompok sebagai calon untuk disaring: setiap satu dinyahpepenjuruankan, *dipangkas* kepada konfigurasi yang membawa berat terbesar, dan konfigurasi yang kekal daripada semua kelompok digabungkan serta dinyahpepenjuruankan bersama. Penyahpepenjuruanan gabungan itulah yang tenaganya dilaporkan oleh lelaran, dan output terpangkasnya sendiri menjadi benih bagi lelaran seterusnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The trim SQD implementation is based on joint research from\n"
"the Cleveland Clinic Foundation, RIKEN, and IBM&reg;. If you use this feature in\n"
"your research, also cite the paper. You can find the citation in the\n"
"`CITATION.bib` file, with citation key `merz2026crossing`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pelaksanaan trim SQD berdasarkan penyelidikan bersama daripada\n"
"Cleveland Clinic Foundation, RIKEN, dan IBM&reg;. Jika anda menggunakan ciri ini dalam\n"
"penyelidikan anda, sila rujuk juga kertas tersebut. Anda boleh mendapati petikan dalam\n"
"fail `CITATION.bib`, dengan kunci petikan `merz2026crossing`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more details on the SQD code used in this example, see the [chemistry Hamiltonian tutorial](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization).\n"
msgstr "Untuk butiran lanjut tentang kod SQD yang digunakan dalam contoh ini, lihat [tutorial Hamiltonian kimia](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up the molecule {#set-up-the-molecule}"
msgstr "Sediakan molekul {#set-up-the-molecule}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the loop {#run-the-loop}"
msgstr "Jalankan gelung {#run-the-loop}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One trim SQD iteration does the following:\n"
msgstr "Satu lelaran trim SQD melakukan perkara berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Screening round.** Partition the bitstrings into batches.  Diagonalize each batch and keep the `trim_ratio` fraction of its CI strings, per spin sector, ranked by weight.\n"
msgstr "**Pusingan saringan.** Bahagikan rentetan bit kepada kelompok. Nyahpepenjuruankan setiap kelompok dan simpan pecahan `trim_ratio` bagi rentetan CI-nya, bagi setiap sektor spin, disusun mengikut berat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Merged round.** Diagonalize the merged survivors once. This is the result the iteration reports, and its own trimmed strings seed the next iteration.\n"
msgstr "**Pusingan gabungan.** Nyahpepenjuruankan konfigurasi gabungan yang kekal sekali. Ini ialah hasil yang dilaporkan oleh lelaran, dan rentetan terpangkasnya sendiri menjadi benih bagi lelaran seterusnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The loop's `sci_solver` performs both rounds, and defaults to this package's PySCF solver.\n"
msgstr "`sci_solver` gelung melakukan kedua-dua pusingan, dan secara lalai menggunakan penyelesai PySCF pakej ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enable trim SQD by passing the `TrimPolicy` as follows:\n"
msgstr "Dayakan trim SQD dengan menghantar `TrimPolicy` seperti berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check whether screening is helping {#check-whether-screening-is-helping}"
msgstr "Semak sama ada saringan membantu {#check-whether-screening-is-helping}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Screening has the most to offer when the sampled configurations greatly outnumber what can be diagonalized at once, so that ranking a larger pool genuinely finds configurations a single batch would have missed. It has the least to offer when a subspace of the affordable size already captures most of the wavefunction.\n"
msgstr "Saringan paling bermanfaat apabila konfigurasi yang disampel jauh melebihi bilangan yang boleh dinyahpepenjuruankan sekali gus, supaya menyusun kumpulan yang lebih besar benar-benar menemui konfigurasi yang akan terlepas oleh satu kelompok. Ia kurang bermanfaat apabila subruang bersaiz yang mampu ditanggung sudah menangkap sebahagian besar fungsi gelombang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Screening depends on the batches differing from one another. `TrimPolicy` manages this by modifying the behavior of `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` to draw one pool of `samples_per_batch * num_batches` bitstrings and partitioning it among the batches, so no bitstring appears in more than one.\n"
msgstr "Saringan bergantung pada kelompok yang berbeza antara satu sama lain. `TrimPolicy` mengurusnya dengan mengubah suai tingkah laku `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` untuk melukis satu kumpulan `samples_per_batch * num_batches` rentetan bit dan membahagikannya antara kelompok, supaya tiada rentetan bit muncul dalam lebih daripada satu kelompok.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bound the subspace {#bound-the-subspace}"
msgstr "Hadkan subruang {#bound-the-subspace}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A subspace here is spanned by the *Cartesian product* of a spin-alpha and a spin-beta CI string array.\n"
msgstr "Subruang di sini direntangi oleh *hasil darab Cartes* bagi tatasusunan rentetan CI spin-alfa dan spin-beta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trimming ranks configurations, but the carryover is two per-spin string lists. Keeping the 150 highest-weight configurations of a subspace typically involves close to 150 distinct alpha strings and 150 distinct beta strings, whose product spans roughly 22,500 configurations, not 150. So the subspace handed to the next iteration is generally much larger than the set that was ranked, and it grows quadratically in what you retain.\n"
msgstr "Pemangkasan menyusun konfigurasi, tetapi bawaan ialah dua senarai rentetan bagi setiap spin. Mengekalkan 150 konfigurasi berat tertinggi bagi satu subruang lazimnya melibatkan hampir 150 rentetan alfa yang berbeza dan 150 rentetan beta yang berbeza, yang hasil darabnya merentangi kira-kira 22,500 konfigurasi, bukan 150. Oleh itu, subruang yang diserahkan kepada lelaran seterusnya biasanya jauh lebih besar daripada set yang disusun, dan ia membesar secara kuadratik mengikut apa yang anda kekalkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trimming and carrying over are bounded separately, because they happen at different points: trimming shrinks each batch of the screening round, while the carryover is what crosses into the next iteration.\n"
msgstr "Pemangkasan dan bawaan dihadkan secara berasingan, kerana ia berlaku pada titik yang berbeza: pemangkasan mengecilkan setiap kelompok pusingan saringan, manakala bawaan ialah apa yang dibawa ke lelaran seterusnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Four arguments bound it, and it is useful to set at least one:\n"
msgstr "Empat argumen menghadkannya, dan adalah berguna untuk menetapkan sekurang-kurangnya satu:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`trim_ratio`** is the fraction of each batch's strings, per spin sector, that survive screening. Lower values shrink the merged subspace but discard configurations the next iteration must rediscover by sampling.\n"
msgstr "**`trim_ratio`** ialah pecahan rentetan setiap kelompok, bagi setiap sektor spin, yang kekal selepas saringan. Nilai yang lebih rendah mengecilkan subruang gabungan tetapi membuang konfigurasi yang mesti ditemui semula oleh lelaran seterusnya melalui pensampelan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`max_strings_per_trim`** caps the strings each batch contributes, per sector, regardless of the ratio. Useful with `symmetrize_spin`, which merges both spin sectors into one list and so roughly doubles what each batch offers. This bound is **per batch**: the merged subspace can hold up to `num_batches` times as many strings, less whatever the batches had in common, which in practice is not much.\n"
msgstr "**`max_strings_per_trim`** menghadkan rentetan yang disumbangkan oleh setiap kelompok, bagi setiap sektor, tanpa mengira nisbah. Berguna dengan `symmetrize_spin`, yang menggabungkan kedua-dua sektor spin ke dalam satu senarai dan dengan itu menggandakan kira-kira apa yang ditawarkan oleh setiap kelompok. Had ini adalah **bagi setiap kelompok**: subruang gabungan boleh memuatkan sehingga `num_batches` kali ganda bilangan rentetan, ditolak apa-apa yang sama antara kelompok, yang dalam praktiknya tidak banyak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`carryover_threshold`**, **`carryover_ratio`**, and **`max_carryover`** bound the strings that seed the next iteration, applied to the merged subspace as a whole rather than per batch. `carryover_threshold` is the amplitude cutoff that `StandardPolicy` uses, with the same default; the other two bound the count, which the cutoff alone does not.\n"
msgstr "**`carryover_threshold`**, **`carryover_ratio`**, dan **`max_carryover`** menghadkan rentetan yang menjadi benih bagi lelaran seterusnya, dikenakan pada subruang gabungan secara keseluruhan dan bukan bagi setiap kelompok. `carryover_threshold` ialah ambang amplitud yang digunakan oleh `StandardPolicy`, dengan nilai lalai yang sama; dua yang lain menghadkan bilangan, yang tidak dapat dilakukan oleh ambang sahaja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`max_dim`**, on `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` itself, bounds each spin sector of every subspace the loop diagonalizes, including the merged one. It acts as a backstop and applies to whatever the policy returns, after the carryover is merged with fresh samples.\n"
msgstr "**`max_dim`**, pada `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` itu sendiri, menghadkan setiap sektor spin bagi setiap subruang yang dinyahpepenjuruankan oleh gelung, termasuk subruang gabungan. Ia bertindak sebagai sandaran dan terpakai pada apa sahaja yang dikembalikan oleh dasar, selepas bawaan digabungkan dengan sampel baharu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The run above sets `max_strings_per_trim=250` and `max_dim=250` together, so neither what each batch contributes nor the subspace built from it can run away.\n"
msgstr "Larian di atas menetapkan `max_strings_per_trim=250` dan `max_dim=250` bersama-sama, supaya sumbangan setiap kelompok mahupun subruang yang dibina daripadanya tidak dapat berkembang tanpa kawalan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use an external eigensolver {#use-an-external-eigensolver}"
msgstr "Gunakan penyelesai eigen luaran {#use-an-external-eigensolver}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can use trim SQD with an external eigensolver by passing the `sci_solver` argument:\n"
msgstr "Anda boleh menggunakan trim SQD dengan penyelesai eigen luaran dengan menghantar argumen `sci_solver`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The prior snippet requires the `sbd-eigensolver` package to be installed from PyPI.\n"
msgstr "Coretan sebelumnya memerlukan pakej `sbd-eigensolver` dipasang daripada PyPI.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Distribute the work {#distribute-the-work}"
msgstr "Agihkan kerja {#distribute-the-work}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `TrimPolicy`, the loop calls `sci_solver` twice per iteration: once with all the batches, and once with the merged subspace. Both calls go through the ordinary `sci_solver` interface, which [this package's multi-process support](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/hpc-acceleration) invokes collectively on every MPI rank.\n"
msgstr "Dengan `TrimPolicy`, gelung memanggil `sci_solver` dua kali bagi setiap lelaran: sekali dengan semua kelompok, dan sekali dengan subruang gabungan. Kedua-dua panggilan melalui antara muka `sci_solver` biasa, yang dipanggil secara kolektif pada setiap pangkat MPI oleh [sokongan berbilang proses pakej ini](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/hpc-acceleration).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two levels of parallelism are potentially available, and they are independent:\n"
msgstr "Dua tahap keselarian berpotensi tersedia, dan keduanya bebas:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Within a diagonalization.** A solver such as SBD can spread a single diagonalization across ranks.\n"
msgstr "**Dalam satu penyahpepenjuruanan.** Penyelesai seperti SBD boleh menyebarkan satu penyahpepenjuruanan merentasi beberapa pangkat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Across the batches.** A solver could, in principle, diagonalize the batches concurrently.\n"
msgstr "**Merentasi kelompok.** Penyelesai pada dasarnya boleh menyahpepenjuruankan kelompok secara serentak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Given a set of batches, the solver determines how to delegate work to its worker processes.\n"
msgstr "Dengan satu set kelompok, penyelesai menentukan cara mewakilkan kerja kepada proses pekerjanya.\n"
